# spec 05a T1 `a2a data pack`: a pinned <XC-id>@<version> this checkout
# cannot resolve is refused LOCALLY — pack is write-free
# by design (its own synopsis: "write-free") and this wave's own policy
# (cmd/a2a/wire.go's resolveDataDeps) does not sync the mirror or resolve a
# credential for it, so the refusal is exec-able against this local
# fixture without ever reaching a GitHub host, matching submit_refusal.txtar
# in this same directory.
mkdir srcdir
! exec a2a data pack --contract XC-axon-widget@1.0.0 --from srcdir --profile synthetic --format json
# B42 (P12 wave G3) split the one message this used to assert into two, and
# this fixture models the FIRST of them. Its mirror carries no descriptor for
# XC-axon-widget at all, so the resolver cannot tell "never published" from
# "not synced yet" — and P-1 says do not collapse those. It therefore reports
# the actionable one. The "never published" branch is claimed only on POSITIVE
# evidence (the mirror's own descriptor already at or past the requested
# version, with no publish event naming it), which this fixture deliberately
# does not seed; internal/space/data_resolve_test.go covers that branch.
stderr 'contract version is not in the local mirror'
